<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" target="global_ai_race_and_gover::regulatory_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Broad sanctions and export controls on dual-use technologies create precedents and political pressure that prompt governments and blocs to expand AI-related export controls, reporting rules, and oversight, raising overall regulatory attention.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_ai_race_and_gover</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" target="global_energy_supply_sho::crossborder_trade_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">New or tightened sanctions (banking, insurance, port access and shipping restrictions) directly block and delay shipments and financial settlement for diesel exports from affected suppliers, immediately reducing cross-border diesel flows.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" target="us_china_strategic_compe::export_control_stringenc" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Heightened sanctions regimes around the Russia–Ukraine war prompt governments to broaden and harden export‑control licensing and enforcement to prevent sanctioned diversion and close loopholes, leading to tighter controls that are then extended to technologies affecting US–China flows.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_strategic_compe</data>
</edge>
