<edge source="us_china_strategic_compe::trade_restriction_level" target="global_ai_race_and_gover::commercialization_pressu" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher bilateral trade barriers shrink foreign market access and supply options, creating stronger domestic market and investor incentives to accelerate commercialization and scale local AI products to substitute for blocked imports.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_compe</data>
  <data key="d40">global_ai_race_and_gover</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_strategic_compe::trade_restriction_level" target="global_energy_supply_sho::crossborder_trade_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in bilateral trade restrictions (tariffs, quotas, export bans or sanctions) directly limits permissible shipments and adds clearance/insurance frictions, immediately reducing volumes of diesel and related distillates moved across borders.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_compe</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_strategic_compe::trade_restriction_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Escalating US trade restrictions on China generate economic backlash among U.S. partners with large China exposure, creating policy rifts and bargaining frictions that weaken coordination and unity within the coalition responding to Russia.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_compe</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
