<edge source="us_china_strategic_compe::export_control_stringenc" target="global_ai_race_and_gover::deployment_scale" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Tighter export controls immediately restrict access to advanced GPUs, NPU accelerators and associated tooling for targeted firms, directly reducing their ability to train and operate large AI models at scale.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_compe</data>
  <data key="d40">global_ai_race_and_gover</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_strategic_compe::export_control_stringenc" target="global_energy_supply_sho::refinery_util_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Tighter export controls on specialty catalysts, control systems and spare parts used in refining constrain access to critical inputs and maintenance supplies, causing unplanned outages and reduced run‑rates at affected refineries over time.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_compe</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_strategic_compe::export_control_stringenc" target="middle_east_iran_houthis::kinetic_attack_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Tighter export controls (notably on dual‑use components) prompt alternative, covert transfers by actors seeking to evade sanctions—accelerating deliveries of drone/missile components to Iran and its Houthi proxies and enabling more frequent/higher‑capability strikes.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_compe</data>
  <data key="d40">middle_east_iran_houthis</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_strategic_compe::export_control_stringenc" target="russia_ukraine_war::arms_transfer_volume" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Tighter export controls on dual‑use technologies and upstream components reduce the availability of chips, guidance components and other inputs that China (and intermediaries) could re‑export or supply to Russian weapons producers, directly lowering the volume and tempo of arms and munitions reaching the conflict theatre.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
