<edge source="middle_east_iran_houthis::maritime_disruption_leve" target="global_ai_race_and_gover::commercialization_pressu" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Acute interruptions to shipping and supply chains raise short‑term costs and investor pressure for rapid revenue growth, incentivizing startups and firms to accelerate AI product launches and monetization to shore up returns.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_iran_houthis</data>
  <data key="d40">global_ai_race_and_gover</data>
</edge>
<edge source="middle_east_iran_houthis::maritime_disruption_leve" target="global_energy_supply_sho::crossborder_trade_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Attacks, seizures, inspections and mine risks in regional sea lanes and at ports force vessel reroutes, cancellations and port closures, directly reducing the volume of diesel/distillate shipments between regions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_iran_houthis</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
</edge>
<edge source="middle_east_iran_houthis::maritime_disruption_leve" target="russia_ukraine_war::arms_transfer_volume" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained Red Sea/Gulf of Aden interdiction forces rerouting, container and RO/RO shipment delays, and spikes in insurance/logistics costs that concretely delay or reduce sea-borne deliveries of weapons and heavy equipment destined for Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_iran_houthis</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="middle_east_iran_houthis::maritime_disruption_leve" target="us_china_strategic_compe::supply_chain_resilience" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Houthi interdictions and attacks on commercial shipping in the Red Sea and Gulf of Aden force large-scale rerouting, port congestion and longer transit times, directly degrading the robustness and adaptive capacity of cross‑border supply chains for autos, semiconductors and other sectors.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_iran_houthis</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_strategic_compe</data>
</edge>
